  "notes": "Drawn from one photo from below and behind the left wing (N657JB at Fort Lauderdale; the file's title dates it 2025-11-17, its metadata 2026-10-17). An art livery: only the big colour masses are areas, each drawn as one rounded blob where the photo has a cluster of shapes on the blue, so the jet reads as blue ahead and many-coloured aft; their edges are approximate (low). The crown isn't seen from below: the masses are carried up over it. The fin's teal fronds are straight bands as the photo shows them; only three of the dozen are drawn. The belly reads '¡SOMOS BORICUA!' (JetBlue's release; the lead called the jet 'Yo Soy Boricua'); its direction (which end it starts) isn't certain from an oblique view. 'Isla del Bluencanto' (the aircraft's name, small white script under the cockpit) and the registration aren't drawn. The right side isn't seen."
